#
# holt — Scala for a ctags that does not have it.
#
# Loaded ONLY after holt has MEASURED that this toolchain cannot extract Scala symbols, and
# defined under a PRIVATE name. Both matter, and the reason is not hypothetical: this definition
# used to live in the always-loaded pack under the real name `Scala`, and the moment upstream
# ctags gained its own Scala parser the load became FATAL — "Language \"Scala\" already
# defined", ctags exits, and holt gets ZERO symbols from EVERY file in the repository. Silence,
# which reads as "these agents share nothing".
#
# A private name cannot collide with a builtin. The measurement gate means a real builtin parser
# is never replaced by these regexes when one exists.
#
### Scala ######################################################################
--langdef=HoltScala
--map-HoltScala=+.scala
--map-HoltScala=+.sc
--kinddef-HoltScala=f,function,methods
--kinddef-HoltScala=c,class,classes objects and traits
--kinddef-HoltScala=v,variable,values
--regex-HoltScala=/^[ \t]*(private|protected|final|override|implicit|inline|[ \t])*def[ \t]+([a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z0-9_]*)/\2/f/
--regex-HoltScala=/^[ \t]*(private|protected|final|sealed|abstract|implicit|case|[ \t])*(class|object|trait|enum)[ \t]+([a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z0-9_]*)/\3/c/
--regex-HoltScala=/^[ \t]*(private|protected|final|implicit|lazy|[ \t])*(val|var)[ \t]+([a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z0-9_]*)/\3/v/
--regex-HoltScala=/^[ \t]*type[ \t]+([a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z0-9_]*)/\1/c/
